# A fixture whose CONTENT is a test's input stays out of the formatter's scope.
#
# four-mistakes.html is served to a real browser and its accessibility tree IS
# the input to scripts/eval-generation-fixture.ts, which asserts on an exact
# computed name — "Expand WS-ALPHA More options", concatenated from the
# treeitem's nested controls. Whitespace between inline elements is capable of
# changing that string, so a formatter has no business in this file.
#
# Measured 2026-09-19: today prettier only expands the CSS inside <style>, and
# the eval's output is byte-identical either way. That safety is INCIDENTAL, not
# structural — it holds because prettier confines itself to <style>, and a
# future version that reflowed the body would change a computed name with
# nothing to warn anyone.
